{{D|Viral}} increases damage to health up to 325% with multiple stacks for a short duration.|In-game Description}}
'''{{D|Viral}} Damage''' is one of the six secondary elemental damage types, composed of {{D|Cold}} and {{D|Toxin}} elements. Deals increased damage to {{D|Orokin}}, but reduced damage to {{D|Infested Deimos}} and {{D|The Murmur}}, with some Deimos units being outright immune. Its [[Status Effect]] increases damage dealt to [[Health]].

==[[Status Effect]]==
===General===
The status effect of {{D|Viral}} damage is '''Virus'''. It amplifies damage to the [[health]] of the afflicted target by '''100%''' for '''6''' seconds. Subsequent procs add '''25%''' increased damage to health up to '''325%''' in total after '''10''' stacks, with each stack having their own duration. Any stacks applied after the 10th will replace the oldest stack. This effect will work even when the health is protected by [[armor]] ("yellow health"); only [[shield]]s and [[overguard]]s are not affected.

<math>
{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Resultant Damage to Health} &= \text{Modded Damage} \times [2 + (0.25 \times (\text{Number of Viral Stacks} - 1) ) ]
\end{aligned}
}
</math>
::''Calculating resultant damage if at least one Viral proc is on target. [[Damage Vulnerability]] provided by Viral procs are multiplicative with other damage bonuses.''

For status effects that apply damage over time (e.g. {{D|Slash}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Gas}}), the damage dealt by the proc throughout its duration is calculated based on whether or not a {{D|Viral}} proc is active when the DoT tick deals damage. For example, a weapon with 100 damage that applies a {{D|Slash}} proc, if the target has 1 {{D|Viral}} proc, will deal 200 damage, then '''70''' damage per second from {{D|Slash}}'s '''Bleed''' until the {{D|Viral}} effect ends, when it will go down to '''35''' per second. If the target does not have a {{D|Viral}} proc initially, the '''Bleed''' damage will be '''35''' per second until the target takes a {{D|Viral}} proc, which will then multiply the DoT accordingly to '''70''' per second. This means that the multiplier is ''not'' applied twice to DoTs, unlike [[Faction Damage Mods|faction damage multipliers]].

Enemies afflicted by a {{D|Viral}} proc are coated in a flowing, leaking miasma of the Energy color of the weapon that inflicted it.

*The following enemies are immune to {{D|Viral}} status:
**[[Ambulas]]
**[[Deimos Carnis]]
**[[Deimos Carnis#Variants|Deimos Carnis Rex]]
**[[Deimos Genetrix]]
**[[Deimos Jugulus]]
**[[Leaping Thrasher#Variants|Deimos Leaping Thrasher]]
**[[Deimos Therid]]
**[[Deimos Saxum]]
**[[Deimos Saxum#Variants|Deimos Saxum Rex]]
**[[Demolisher Boiler]]
**[[Demolisher Thrasher]]
**[[Tusk Bolkor]]
**[[Tusk Firbolg]]
**[[Techrot Babau]]
*The following enemies are completely immune to {{D|Viral}}:
**[[Demolisher Charger]]
**[[Demolisher Juggernaut]]

===Railjack===
{{D|Viral}} does not have a [[Railjack]] space counterpart and is thus not able to proc any status effect nor is it included in calculations for status proc weighting.

